    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15093" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριστ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>,
			ὁ, dual <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριστέοιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					1304
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄριστος</span>):—used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> mostly in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριστῆες</span>
			<i>those who excel in valour,</i>
			
			<i>chiefs,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.404
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρας ἀριστῆας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.218
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.81
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1a
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				9.107
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ant.Lib.
				2.2
			</span></i>, etc.: sg., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				306
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρὸς ἀριστέως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					28
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); as an honorary title, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2881
			</span></i> (Milet.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				4.914
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Cibyra</span>).</div>
